{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a1534c-fdac-7428-ab97-0d2c9f906306","toolName":"task","args":{},"result":"{\"lg_name\":\"Command\",\"update\":{\"files\":{},\"filesReadTrace\":[\"/home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol\",\"/home/user/app/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\",\"/home/user/app/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\"],\"messages\":[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"content\":\"High — `no-corpus-rule` — `withdraw` can silently burn user refund credit if `settler` is unset\\n**Location:** DemandPool.sol:149, DemandPool.withdraw\\n**Uncatalogued:** The loaded access-control and input-validation rules cover authorization and caller-controlled parameters, but none covers external calls to an uninitialized dependency address that succeed with no effect and orphan funds.\\n**Why it matters:** `withdraw` removes the buyer from `_buyers` / `_buyerIndex` first, then credits the refund via `ISettler(settler).creditWithdrawal(...)`. If `settler` is still `address(0)`, this external call does not credit any storage and does not revert, so the user is de-registered but receives no claimable balance. Their deposited collateral remains in the pool and is no longer attributable to them through normal settlement/refund paths, creating permanent fund loss for that user flow.\\n**Fix:** Enforce dependency initialization before any flow that relies on it: require `settlerSet == true` (and `settler != address(0)`) in `commit` and `withdraw`, and/or revert in `withdraw` unless `settler` is configured. Prefer explicit interface/liveness checks during setup and fail-closed behavior before mutating buyer state.\\n\\n## Files Read\\n| File | Read |\\n|---|---|\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol | yes |\\n\\n## Audit Provenance\\n| Subagent | Dispatched | Files audited | Corpus rules cited |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| solidity-auditor | yes | 5 | no-corpus-rule |\",\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_016SZGFSatj9V6bELDY7M3eT\",\"name\":\"task\",\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}]},\"goto\":[]}"}}
