{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a1534e-33da-704e-b97f-c4a996237f1d","toolName":"task","args":{},"result":"{\"lg_name\":\"Command\",\"update\":{\"files\":{},\"messages\":[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"content\":\"## Findings\\n1. [High] impossible-settlement-parameters-allowed — `postDeal` accepts deal configs that can never satisfy settlement conditions  \\n   Criterion: 1 functional  \\n   Location: `contracts/DealFactory.sol:DealFactory.postDeal` (line approx 63)  \\n   Why it matters: The factory does not enforce `minBuyers <= cap` (or that tier thresholds are reachable under `cap`). A supplier can post a deal where settlement is mathematically impossible, so the requested settle flow is unreachable for that deal and users can only wait for refund after deadline.  \\n   Suggested fix: In `postDeal`, add validation that `cap > 0`, `minBuyers <= cap`, and `tiers[tiers.length - 1].minBuyers <= cap` (and/or whichever tier reachability invariant your product expects). Revert early on impossible configurations.\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Assumed user intent is that posted deals should be genuinely settle-able when demand is sufficient, not intentionally “refund-only” configurations.\\n\\n## Audit Provenance\\n| Subagent | Dispatched | Files audited | Corpus rules cited |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| functional-auditor | yes | 4 | — |\",\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01C52dwPQqRET78VtcQgjMcs\",\"name\":\"task\",\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}]},\"goto\":[]}"}}
