{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a1534f-557a-700a-8161-c9ec86cc4955","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/contracts/references/static-analysis.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\nrotected selfdestruct, arbitrary ETH/ERC20 transfers.\\n   170\\t- **Medium** — Potential issues depending on context. Review carefully. Examples: unchecked return values, dangerous strict equality, weak randomness.\\n   171\\t- **Low** — Minor concerns. Address if straightforward.\\n   172\\t- **Informational/Optimization** — Usually safe to ignore (for example, `pragma`, `dead-code`, `solc-version`, `too-many-digits`).\\n   173\\t\\n   174\\t## After Analysis\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\t1. Read the JSON file and present findings to the user grouped by severity, with file locations and line numbers.\\n   177\\t2. For High/Medium issues: explain the vulnerability and offer to fix it.\\n   178\\t3. After you apply fixes, re-compile and re-run Slither to confirm the issue is resolved.\\n   179\\t4. Do not deploy contracts with unresolved High-severity findings unless the user explicitly accepts the risk.\\n   180\\t\\n   181\\t## Common False Positives to Exclude\\n   182\\t\\n   183\\tThese detectors often produce noise in this sandbox environment:\\n   184\\t- `naming-convention` — style preference, not security\\n   185\\t- `solc-version` — sandbox uses a fixed solc version\\n   186\\t- `pragma` — single-file analysis does not need pragma checks\\n   187\\t\\n   188\\t## Troubleshooting\\n   189\\t\\n   190\\tThe toolchain is pre-installed in the template. The sandbox runs as an unprivileged user with no `sudo`. If a binary is genuinely missing, reinstall into `$HOME/.local/bin`. Never install into `/usr/local/bin`, and never use `apt-get` or `sudo` — both fail in this sandbox.\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\t**`slither: error: unrecognized arguments: ...`** means the command used a flag that does not exist. This exits with code 2 before Slither compiles anything. Check the flag names in this document. `--solc-evm-version` and a bare `--evm-version` do not exist. See \\\"Key Flags\\\" above.\\n   193\\t\\n   194\\t**`Multiple frameworks detected: Foundry, solc, Solc-json. Using Foundry (highest priority).`** is informational, not an error. It confirms Slither is running `forge build` and reading `foundry.toml` and `remappings.txt`. See \\\"Foundry projects\\\" above.\\n   195\\t\\n   196\\t**Install uv (Python package manager):**\\n   197\\t```bash\\n   198\\tcurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/0.11.8/install.sh | sh && export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\\\"\\n   199\\t```\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t**Install slither-analyzer (requires uv):**\\n   202\\t```bash\\n   203\\t\\\"$HOME/.local/bin/uv\\\" tool install slither-analyzer && export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\\\"\\n   204\\t```\\n   205\\t\\n   206\\t**Install native solc binary:**\\n   207\\t```bash\\n   208\\tcurl -L https://github.com/ethereum/solidity/releases/download/v0.8.28/solc-static-linux -o \\\"$HOME/.local/bin/solc\\\" && chmod +x \\\"$HOME/.local/bin/solc\\\"\\n   209\\t```\\n   210\\t\\n   211\\t**Full reinstall (everything from scratch):**\\n   212\\t```bash\\n   213\\tcurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/0.11.8/install.sh | sh && \\\"$HOME/.local/bin/uv\\\" tool install slither-analyzer && export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\\\" && curl -L https://github.com/ethereum/solidity/releases/download/v0.8.28/solc-static-linux -o \\\"$HOME/.local/bin/solc\\\" && chmod +x \\\"$HOME/.local/bin/solc\\\"\\n   214\\t```\\n   215\\t\\n   216\\t## Limitations\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t- Slither requires the contract to compile. If analysis fails, check compilation first.\\n   219\\t- The sandbox has native `solc` 0.8.28. A contract that needs a different compiler version can fail.\\n   220\\t- For complex cross-contract interactions across multiple files, target the project root (`.`) with `--filter-paths node_modules`.\\n   221\\t- A contract that needs a Cancun-only opcode, such as `mcopy` (used by OpenZeppelin 5.2 and later in `Clones.sol` and `Bytes.sol`), cannot compile under the project's Paris pin. See \\\"Foundry projects\\\" above for how to report this.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01CBrFfVJDhYJNx8kKxJfT3G\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.12\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
